# RemoSound

Python CLI that bulk-downloads MyInstants sound effects into `downloads/` and
matches them to Remotion scenes. `run.py` is the only entrypoint — extend it
instead of adding scripts.

## Environment

Dependencies live in `.venv/`. The canonical spelling is the explicit
interpreter path; `.venv\Scripts\activate` shortens it to `python`.

Raw PowerShell is broken on this host (a `caveman shrink` hook rejects bare
`git ...` / `python ...` with `Unexpected token 'shrink'`). Wrap every shell
command in `cmd /c "..."` and use `&`, never `&&`, inside one call:

```bat
cmd /c "git status"
cmd /c ".venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q"
```

## Commands

```bat
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --trending --limit 20
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --category memes --limit 20
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --search "boom" --limit 20
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --match "explosion in the distance, dust settling"
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --rebuild-index
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q
```

`run.py` with no flags opens the interactive menu.

## Module map

`run.py` → `cli` → `matcher` / `remotion_adapter`, behind
`scraper` → `downloader` → `storage`. Lower layers never import `cli`.

## Hard rules

- Max 5 concurrent downloads (`--max-concurrency` only lowers it), ≥0.5 s
  between page fetches, exponential backoff on HTTP 429 (0.5 s, 1 s, 2 s, then
  give up after 3 retries).
- Never re-download anything already in `downloads/manifest.json`; partial
  files use `.part` and are removed on failure.
- Sanitize every filename for Windows and never produce an empty stem.
- `downloads/` and `sound-bank.json` are runtime data, not source — never
  commit or hand-edit them.
- Audio is community-uploaded MyInstants content; verify rights before
  commercial use (see `README.md`).
